  "worked_solution": "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)^{4}+6 & <18 \\\\ 2(x+4)^{4} & <12 \\\\ (x+4)^{4} & <6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(x+4)^{4}} & <\\sqrt[4]{6} \\\\ |x+4| & <\\sqrt[4]{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt[4]{6}<x+4<\\sqrt[4]{6}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[4]{6}<x+4 & <\\sqrt[4]{6} \\\\ -\\sqrt[4]{6}-4<x & <\\sqrt[4]{6}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
